From ddf1b7547680a35ee32a4485500445a928daeb3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:18:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Map growth: keeper ExtendFrontier candidate and prize ceiling
 refusal

Keeper (local candidate, off by default): with `extend = true` the rings
duty sends ExtendFrontier(effective r_max + 1) only when the program's
rule holds (fclient::land::frontier_extend_check mirrors proc/map.rs:
a ceiling, d <= ceiling, Running, every ring opened, a bell since the
last opening, some wedge crowded past theta), the outermost ring is
complete and folded by a later bell, and d <= extend_max_ring (default
17, the prize program's MAX_RING; the keeper cannot see a pool). d is
recomputed from the chain every tick; the engine dedups by key and
treats AlreadyDone as landed. The open-ring policy now uses the
effective r_max so the extended ring is opened. frontier-stack gains
--keeper-extend and --r-max-ceiling (conquest only; <= 17 with
--prize-so).

Prize: InitPool refuses a season whose r_max_ceiling exceeds MAX_RING
with CeilingPastTally (0x111). The ring-17 limit is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
